Subject: [PATCH] pvrsgx 1.6: dump EDM task registers at hardware recovery

The SGX lockup watchdog (SGXOSTimer) declares a hang only when the EDM task
register it samples -- psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg0, optionally XOR
ui32EDMTaskReg1 -- is unchanged for three consecutive samples. That progress
signal is never recorded, so the recovery log cannot show whether the
microkernel task counter was genuinely frozen or merely advancing slowly.

Dump both EDM task registers (address and value) in SGXDumpDebugInfo, which runs
before SGXReset. Identical values across consecutive recoveries confirm a real
microkernel stall; changing values indicate the uKernel is still progressing and
the watchdog is firing early.

Reads hardware registers only; unlike PVRSRV_USSE_EDM_STATUS_DEBUG /
PVRSRV_DUMP_MK_TRACE it does not depend on the microkernel build options (which
would fail the fatal KM/microkernel build-options check against the release
ukernel). Diagnostic only.
---
 .../drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c   | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
index 3f348c4f8..3d2fd1dd6 100755
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
@@ -976,0 +977,7 @@ static IMG_VOID SGXDumpDebugInfo (PVRSRV_SGXDEV_INFO	*psDevInfo,
+			PVR_LOG(("(P%u) EDM_TASK_REG0 [0x%03X]: %08X", ui32CoreNum, psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg0,
+					OSReadHWReg(psDevInfo->pvRegsBaseKM, SGX_MP_CORE_SELECT(psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg0, ui32CoreNum))));
+			if (psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg1 != 0)
+			{
+				PVR_LOG(("(P%u) EDM_TASK_REG1 [0x%03X]: %08X", ui32CoreNum, psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg1,
+						OSReadHWReg(psDevInfo->pvRegsBaseKM, SGX_MP_CORE_SELECT(psDevInfo->ui32EDMTaskReg1, ui32CoreNum))));
+			}
